            </section>
            <section>
               <title value="Hospital course note"/>
               <code>
                  <coding>
                     <system value="http://loinc.org"/>
                     <code value="8648-8"/>
                     <display value="Hospital course note"/>
                  </coding>
               </code>
               <text>
                  <status value="generated"/>
                  <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Dear colleague, I am writing to inform you regarding your patient, a 75-year-old female admitted on 25/07/2009 with an acute exacerbation of her known chronic obstructive pulmonary disease. On admission, she presented with increased dyspnoea, productive cough, and reduced oxygen saturation. Clinical examination, chest X-ray, arterial blood gas analysis, and pulse oximetry confirmed the exacerbation. Blood tests were obtained to exclude infection and metabolic disturbance. She was treated with nebulised bronchodilators, systemic corticosteroids, and supplemental oxygen therapy, resulting in satisfactory clinical improvement. Physiotherapy for airway clearance was initiated, and patient education regarding inhaler technique and disease self-management was provided prior to discharge. She was discharged on 26/07/2009 in a stable condition. Please arrange close follow-up and review of her maintenance inhaler regimen. Do not hesitate to contact me for further information.</div>
               </text>
            </section>
